# Every text file is checked out with LF line endings on every platform.
#
# Three committed artefacts are compared BYTE FOR BYTE against what a fresh run
# produces: lab/local/runs/latest/RUN-MANIFEST.json and its inputs (each input
# is SHA-256 digested into the manifest), everything under lab/ch06/fixtures and
# lab/ch06/runs/latest, and the evaluation card. With Git's default
# `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows those files are checked out with CRLF, the
# digests move, and both lab checks fail on a clean clone for a reason that has
# nothing to do with the detector. The scripts now write LF bytes on every
# platform; this is the other half, which makes the checkout match.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git detect binaries by content. There are no binary files
# in the tree today; a committed binary must be listed below with `-text` so
# that detection is never the only thing standing between it and a line-ending
# rewrite.
* text=auto eol=lf

# No binaries are committed. When one is added, declare it here, for example:
#   *.png -text
#   *.ico -text
